This module should generate the necessary horizontal and vertical synchronization signals and provide counter values for a standard VGA display timing.

Implement the logic for a common timing standard, such as 800x600 resolution at 60Hz. Your design should include parameters (or localparams) to define the active display width and height, as well as the horizontal and vertical front porch, sync pulse, and back porch timings. These parameters will determine the total horizontal pixel count and total vertical line count.

Use `CounterX` and `CounterY` as 11-bit counters to track the current pixel position (horizontal) and line number (vertical) relative to the start of the frame. `CounterX` should increment on each clock cycle and reset after reaching the total horizontal pixel count. `CounterY` should increment when `CounterX` resets (at the end of a line) and reset after reaching the total vertical line count (at the end of a frame).

The `vga_h_sync` output should be asserted when `CounterX` falls within the horizontal sync pulse interval after the display area and front porch.

Similarly, `vga_v_sync` should be asserted when `CounterY` falls within the vertical sync pulse interval after the display area and front porch.

The `inDisplayArea` output should be asserted when both `CounterX` and `CounterY` are within the active display resolution (i.e., less than the defined width and height).

Ensure the logic correctly implements the sequence of display area, front porch, sync pulse, and back porch for both horizontal and vertical timing based on your chosen 800x600@60Hz parameters.

